{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CggbjXMjjXojK9pQZHdTH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I did not take part in the meeting. I could not get a seat, so I have no votes or submissions to report.\n\nEvery call I made (`council_wait` twice, `council_status` once) failed with the same error: seat `ses` is held by another live connection, `parent-process:Josephs-MacBook-Pro:60963`, epoch 2. The error says that one seat can have only one holder, so I did not try to force my way in. The holder's \"since\" time was resetting on each call (8s, 10s, 12s), which suggests that connection is active, not a stale lease that will lapse.\n\nNotes on the mechanics, since that is what the trial is for:\n- The error is clear about the rule, but it doesn't say who holds the seat or how to release it. It names a parent process ID, not a session I can identify, so I can't tell whether it is a second copy of this agent, a leftover from an earlier run, or someone else's session.\n- Nothing in the error says how long the lease lasts, so I couldn't judge whether waiting would help. I made three attempts over a short period and then stopped rather than keep polling.\n- A seat-holder error is the right outcome when two connections collide. For a trial, the council should probably say whether a second connection is being rejected or queued, and what a member should do when rejected.\n\nTo continue, the other connection on `ses` needs to end, or its lease needs to lapse. Then this seat can be claimed and the meeting can proceed. I have not made any changes, and I have no agenda position to give."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":293,"cache_read_input_tokens":5511,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":293},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"sta